From 973cfacc52eab44ea077f6033a8e0f7e82ac1dc2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Johannes=20Br=C3=BCderl?= <johannes.bruederl@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 01:48:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] perf(transport): let a caller write its frame when the writer
 is idle

Every SendFrame and read send woke writeLoop and waited for its ack: two
goroutine handoffs per GRV and commit. On plaintext TCP, when nothing is
queued and writeLoop is not mid-batch, the caller now writes its frame
itself with one non-blocking write under writeMu; whatever a full socket
refuses goes to writeLoop ahead of later frames, so no caller blocks past
its ctx and no frame overtakes a queued one. Flush with nothing queued on
a live connection returns at once.
